---
/**
 * THE FIRST THING UNDER THE HERO IS EVIDENCE, AND IT CARRIES THE FIRST PICTURE THIS SITE HAS EVER
 * PUT ON ITS FRONT PAGE.
 *
 * Measured against the live origin on 2026-09-21, the deployed landing had `<img>` 0 and
 * `<video>` 0. Every sentence on it was a claim, including the load-bearing one two sections below
 * — "changes nothing until you say so" — which is the product's central safety promise and was
 * printed in the same typeface as everything else with nothing behind it. The owner's standing
 * instruction for this site is "do not make claims when we can demonstrate them".
 *
 * NOT ONE WORD IN THIS SECTION IS WRITTEN BY THIS FILE. Every quoted string comes out of
 * src/data/consent-proof.ts, which records the file each one was taken from, and
 * tests/proof-is-evidence.test.mjs re-reads those files and fails if a quote is not in the one it
 * names. Two kinds of source, and the difference is the point:
 *
 *   the two access lines and the disclosure  — quoted from apps/apple-plugin/src/init.server.luau,
 *     the SHIPPED plugin's own string literals. A page that reproduces a panel the plugin no longer
 *     renders goes red rather than quietly wrong.
 *   the transcript and the Explorer read-back  — quoted from the record of the run.
 *
 * The heading, the three small labels and the arrow are the only English here that is ours, and
 * they name the structure rather than asserting a result.
 *
 * WHY THE EXPLORER BLOCK IS THE POINT AND NOT DECORATION. A model reporting its own success is not
 * evidence of it. That tree is what Studio's own Explorer showed afterwards, which is why the
 * record kept it and why it is on the page rather than summarised into a tick.
 *
 * THE LIMIT LINE AT THE FOOT IS PART OF THE MEASUREMENT, NOT A DISCLAIMER ON IT. It is the record's
 * own sentence about what it does not establish. Without it this band reads as "Apple is safe";
 * with it, it reads as the one refused operation and one granted one that were actually run. Do not
 * trim it to tighten the layout.
 *
 * THIS IS A COMPONENT RATHER THAN MARKUP IN index.astro, which is the exception to that page's
 * rule that it owns its own sections. It was written while another lane held index.astro in the
 * shared checkout, and a seventy-line insertion into a file somebody else is rewriting is how one
 * lane's commit swallows another's. <Horizon /> is the precedent: a self-contained object with its
 * own reasons gets its own file.
 */
import { CONSENT_PROOF } from '../data/consent-proof';
import ArrowLink from './picks/ArrowLink.astro';
---

<section class="band" id="proof" aria-labelledby="proof-title">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="band-head" data-reveal>
      <h2 id="proof-title" class="section-title">The same request, sent twice</h2>
      <p class="section-sub">{CONSENT_PROOF.summary.text}</p>
    </div>

    <div class="proof">
      <figure class="proof-shot" data-reveal>
        {/* NO `loading="lazy"` ON THIS ONE, DELIBERATELY. It is the first image on the page and on
            a phone it sits within a screen of the fold, where deferring it buys a visible pop-in
            and saves nothing. `width`/`height` are the intrinsic size of the served file so the
            row reserves its box before the bytes land — a proof panel that shoves the transcript
            down when it arrives is worse than no picture. */}
        <img
          src={CONSENT_PROOF.capture.src}
          alt={CONSENT_PROOF.capture.alt}
          width={CONSENT_PROOF.capture.width}
          height={CONSENT_PROOF.capture.height}
          decoding="async"
        />
        <figcaption class="micro proof-caption">Roblox Studio · {CONSENT_PROOF.capturedLabel}</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <div class="proof-pair">
        <p class="proof-ask"><span class="micro proof-ask-label">Sent, both times</span>{CONSENT_PROOF.request.text}</p>

        <div class="proof-runs">
          <article class="proof-run proof-run-refused">
            <p class="micro proof-state">{CONSENT_PROOF.refused.access.text}</p>
            <p class="proof-answer">{CONSENT_PROOF.refused.answer.text}</p>
            <p class="proof-log">{CONSENT_PROOF.refused.log.text}</p>
            <p class="proof-outcome">{CONSENT_PROOF.refused.outcome.text}</p>
          </article>

          <article class="proof-run proof-run-allowed">
            <p class="micro proof-state">{CONSENT_PROOF.allowed.access.text}</p>
            <p class="proof-answer">{CONSENT_PROOF.allowed.answer.text}</p>
            {/* Studio's Explorer, as it read afterwards. `<pre>` because the alignment carries the
                tree, and the string is one quote rather than six so the guard checks the shape of
                the tree and not merely its node names. */}
            <pre class="proof-tree">{CONSENT_PROOF.allowed.tree.text}</pre>
          </article>
        </div>

        <p class="proof-disclosure">{CONSENT_PROOF.disclosure.text}</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    {/* THE WAY OUT OF THE BAND, AND THE REASON IT IS HERE RATHER THAN IN THE PAGE'S OWN HEADER.
        This band is one refused operation and one granted one. /proof is a whole run: the log
        minute by minute, the object counts before and after it, what the game reported when a
        person played the result, and the five things that were wrong with it. A visitor who is
        persuaded by this band has nowhere else to go, and the site has no other route to that page
        from the landing — src/pages/index.astro, which owns this page's header and footer, was
        held open by another lane while this was written, and /showcase spent a night deployed with
        nothing linking to it for exactly that reason. A component this lane owns can carry its own
        door. */}
    <p class="proof-more">
      <ArrowLink href="/proof">The whole log of one run, and the five defects it left behind</ArrowLink>
    </p>

    {/* The limit is the record's own sentence and stays on the page. The record's repository path
        does not: a file path set as marketing copy tells a reader nothing they can open, and the
        whole run it comes from is one link above, on /proof. The path still lives in
        data/consent-proof.ts, where tests/proof-is-evidence.test.mjs re-reads every quote from it. */}
    <p class="micro proof-source">{CONSENT_PROOF.limit.text}</p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  /* Four declarations in their own block rather than a sixth rule in landing.css: that file was
     carrying another lane's uncommitted work at the time, and a link is not worth committing
     somebody else's half-finished stylesheet to ship. `a` is `color: inherit; text-decoration:
     none` site-wide on the landing, so an unstyled anchor here would be invisible as a link. */
  .proof-more {
    margin: 18px 0 0;
    font-size: 13.5px;
    line-height: 21px;
  }

</style>
